      "textEn": "73\nOne can be freed from sins by worshiping in temples, mosques, or churches,\nwith the hope of being freed from the fruits of sins,\nbe careful not to sin intentionally. On the strength of devotional service,\nThis mentality of deliberately committing sins is called Nanho Jorg Yasya Hi Prapabuddhi: and in the path of devotion, this is the greatest offense. Therefore, to be careful of such sinners, hearing is extremely\nnecessary. With the intention of giving special emphasis to this listening method, Shukdev Goswami invokes all welfare.\nHe who is seized by the power of His feet,\nHe who is seated in the midst of the two, the inner self.\nThey realize the state of Brahman, the state of liberation,\nTo Him, O auspicious one, salutations, salutations. 96. Meaning of the word\nVichakshana - very intelligent; Yat - which; Charan-upasadanat - by surrendering at the lotus feet; Sadham - attachment;\nVyudasya - completely renouncing; Ubhayat- in both; Antah- of the self; Vindanti - they progress further; Hi - certainly; Brahm-gatim - towards the spiritual world; Gata-klamah - without difficulty; Tasmai- to that;\nSubhadra- auspicious; Shravase- that which has been heard; TH: - My salutations; Namah- again and again.\n.\nI repeatedly bow to the all-auspicious Lord Shri Krishna.\nJust by taking refuge in his lotus feet, highly intelligent people get rid of all\nattachments of the present and future world, and without any difficulty, they progress towards the spiritual world.\nThat is the meaning.\nThe Lord Shri Krishna has repeatedly advised Arjuna or all those who want to become his exclusive devotees,\nHe has repeatedly given the teaching. In his final sermon in the Bhagavad Gita (18.64-66), he has given a very secret\nsermon--\nListen again to the most secret of all, O Kacha. I desire, I will tell you, then I will tell you what is good. I will not be angry, I will not be pleased, I will not be displeased."
