      "textEn": "[87]\nHe is the husband of all women in his creation, but the bound soul, subdued by God, feels proud to be the husband of one or two\nwives. The various types of husbands described in this verse, these qualities only suit Lord Krishna.\nTherefore, Shukdev Goswami has made a special mention of the Yadav dynasty and its movement. All the members of the Yadav dynasty\nknew that Shri Krishna is everything, and when they ended their divine plays on earth, they all wanted to return to him. The destruction of the Yadu dynasty happened by the will of God,\nbecause its members had to return to the abode of God with God. The destruction of the Yadu dynasty by God\nwas a physical display created, otherwise all the members of the Yadu dynasty and God were constant companions. Therefore,\nGod is the guide of all devotees, that is why Shukdev Goswami, with loving feelings,\nbowed down to God.\nThose who meditate on the unmanifest,\nThey see the essence of the self in the unmanifest.\nThus, the poets speak,\nO Mukunda, may the Lord be pleased. 21. Meaning of the word\n\nYat-angri- whose lotus feet; Abhidhyan-- contemplating every moment; Samadhi- Samadhi; Dhautaya-- from being washed away; Dhiya--\nWith such pure intellect; Anupashyanti- following the great men; Hi- Indeed; Tatvamu- the ultimate truth;\nAtmanah- of the self and the Supreme Soul; Vadanti- say; Cha- also; Etat- this; Kavayah- philosophers or learned scholars; Yatha-\nAs he thinks; Sah- He; Me- Mine; Mukundah- Lord Krishna (the giver of liberation); Bhagavan- God;\nPrasidatam- be pleased with me.. A devotee, by contemplating their lotus feet every moment,\nand by walking on the footsteps of great men, can have a vision of the ultimate truth in Samadhi. However, learned men contemplate them according to their own fancies. May God bless me.\nMeaning: Yogis, after making a difficult effort to control their senses, are situated in the Samadhi of Yoga to get a glimpse of the Supreme Soul residing within 